From 895167cbe567444a8b61c2a57212834b55de90c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:27:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The collapsed mine knocks over its own cargo, carts and
 lanterns (patch 0091)

The finished Deadmines' preview (patch 0087's marker, game object 500100 at
0xF11007A184FFFFFF on map 36) left the mine's own doodads as they were: the neat cargo stacks,
carts and barrows of its review views 3, 9 and 15 stood untouched beside the fall, and a lantern
hung lit right over each pile (views 1 and 15). They are the mine WMO's own doodads, so a server
can't move them.

While the marker stands, the mine's aftermath WMO variant now also clears the models of the
doodads in MINE_DOODADS (their MODD indices, kept: portals and the prop lighting tables index
them), as it clears the ship's, so no prop, collider or interior-light slot is made for them.
For those in DARK_LANTERNS the mine's own lights (MOLT) within LANTERN_REACH (1.6 yd) of the
lantern go to intensity 0: the mine's lanterns carry theirs 0.4 to 1 yd off their pivot and no two
are that close. A dark light is still spawned and named by its rooms, so nothing becomes ungated.
The intact model is untouched: when the marker goes the streamer reloads it, every doodad and
light as it was.

The server sets its own knocked-over, tipped and crooked copies where they stood. Three of the
mine's models have no game-object display, so they join EXTRA_DISPLAYS: 60005 the hanging lantern
(GeneralLantern03), 60006 the ore cart (CaveMineCar01), 60007 the netted cargo
(DeadMineCargoNetBoxes).

HasActionCombat() is 30: the server sends the copies only to this round, so an older client keeps
the mine's own doodads and sees nothing twice. The lists are mirrored in Basin Battle's
htl-map/src/deadmines/aftermath.rs and held to its server plan by a test there.
